  "steps": [
   "The night before, squeeze the juice from the oranges into a large bowl. Stir in the oats, water, raisins, cinnamon and salt.",
   "Coarsely grate the apples, skin and all, straight into the bowl. Stir well so the apple is coated in juice and stays pale. Cover and chill overnight, or for at least 6 hours.",
   "In the morning, halve the grapes and roughly chop the hazelnuts.",
   "Give the oats a good stir. They should be soft and creamy. Add a splash of water if they are thicker than you like.",
   "Fold in half the grapes, then spoon into bowls. Scatter over the rest of the grapes, the hazelnuts and the pumpkin seeds, and eat straight away."
